   "title": "COP texture (read me)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "A small stone-tile texture made with COP (image) nodes. A COP image is a stack of named layers; most nodes read one layer and write another.\n\n1) COP Noise writes a Perlin noise into layer C; COP Levels raises its contrast.\n2) COP Pattern (Tile Pattern, 4 x 4) adds the layers tile (mask), tile_height (bevelled tiles) and tile_rand (one random value per tile).\n3) COP Composite multiplies tile_height by the noise into a new layer 'height' (Opacity 0.35 keeps it subtle).\n4) COP Remap turns tile_rand into a colour per tile (a ramp with r,g,b stops).\n5) COP Height to Normal makes a normal map N from 'height'; COP Light shades the colour with it.\n6) COP Export turns a layer into a ComfyUI IMAGE for Preview / Save (normals with mode 'signed').\n\nTweak: Tile Count, Gap and Bevel, the Levels range, the Remap ramp, the normal Strength and the light direction."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
